  "proof_scope": [
    "Actual scalar marked holomorphic continuation on a connected RHP domain implies abs(Im m)<=abs(arg W)/2<pi/4. The saturated physical curve supplies generic scalar lifts; a full single-valued spectral continuation is not assumed. Compact growth is therefore automatic on a common domain.",
    "A common prime cold-hot marked domain alone would suffice for ETH26 by the previous two-constants theorem. Such a prime common domain is not proved.",
    "For odd square prime powers q=2n+1 with n>exp(100000), the actual hot marked germ has an accessible genuine scalar ramification point with Re(tau)>1/16 and abs(tau)<=1024. This is existential, not a numerical location; sector winding excludes ordinary zeros or poles.",
    "Two saved prime T128 inputs have strictly positive pinned-reflection completions; two T64 inputs have strict negative coordinates. Four canonical Arb224 records independently replay. A kappa floor is not required for direct ordinary theta witnesses.",
    "Actual unrounded projected averages have an explicit all-field raw-positivity horizon O_tau(n^(3/2)). The independent endpoint deficit argument gives one-reflection mean/sector/mark-preserving completion at O_tau(n^(5/4)); the safe constants are not numerically optimized. Both remain beyond the proved marked window.",
    "Uniform weights optimize the specified decreasing-weight absolute endpoint and mean-budget estimates, not every signed weighted construction.",
    "The one-FFT endpoint generator has exact algebraic justification and small direct-implementation checks. Its large proposal remains floating provenance before exact Fourier rounding.",
    "At p7340033 T128, the saved rational Fourier proposal has a rigorously negative repaired minus coordinate 2136334 and a positive plus row. Its Arb128 record independently replays byte-identically. This does not certify an unrounded exact Picard failure, exclude another completion, or disprove eventual feasibility.",
    "Exact affine constraints follow from Fourier support and pinned-projection identities, not interval containment alone. Rounded inputs are not assigned the unrounded Picard mean budget without shadowing.",
    "All proofs are ordinary mathematical audits and exact/interval checks, not Lean kernel proofs. No main-target proof is claimed."
  ],
